    SpecificationOverview
        Type: Section
        Role: Content
        Caption: SIL — Semantic Interface Layer
        Purpose: How SIL replaces raw HTML/DOM scraping and JS execution with pure STF semantics

        CoreMechanism
            Type: Text
            Caption: Agent Web Navigation Without HTML/DOM or JS
            Content: SIL extends STF with an application vocabulary for web pages and interfaces. Agents discover the SIL endpoint via the HTML head link (rel="sil") or visible SIL badges and traverse the site deterministically without rendering DOM trees or running client-side scripts.

        ConformanceProfiles
            Type: Section
            Role: Content
            Caption: The 5 Conformance Profiles of SIL

            Profile1
                Type: Text
                Caption: Profile 1 — Static Content & Navigation
                Content: Read-only semantic page structure, explicit Purpose descriptors, and cross-page Navigate links.

            Profile2
                Type: Text
                Caption: Profile 2 — Structured Discovery & Indexing
                Content: Canonical metadata, typed section roles, and deterministic entity summaries for agent retrieval.

            Profile3
                Type: Text
                Caption: Profile 3 — Parameterized Queries & Forms
                Content: Typed input parameters, constraints, and query targets without DOM form scraping.

            Profile4
                Type: Text
                Caption: Profile 4 — Stateful Actions & Transactions
                Content: Explicit preconditions, state transitions, and confirmation semantics for interactive workflows.

            Profile5
                Type: Text
                Caption: Profile 5 — Multi-Turn Agent Collaboration & Trust Isolation
                Content: Full interactive sessions separating authoritative interface semantics (Origin: System) from untrusted user content (Origin: UserContent).

